<title>RUSSIA: Sayansk Aluminium sees higher output by 1998.</title>
<headline>Sayansk Aluminium sees higher output by 1998.</headline>
<dateline>SAYANOGORSK, Russia 1996-08-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sayansk Aluminium expects annual output to rise by 51,000 tonnes by 1998, from 1996's expected 327,000 tonnes, chief executive Oleg Deripaska told Reuters on Saturday.</p>
<p>A company statement released on Friday said Sayansk planned to increase output to 600,000 tonnes a year in the near future, but it gave no details of exactly when this could happen.</p>
</text>
